# WAI v2 Phase 3 — Skills Directory + Extension Identity

**Teaching type:** Implementation instructions
**For AI assistants:** This is Phase 3 of the WAI v2 migration. Do not start this phase unless Phase 2 is confirmed complete in WAI-MIGRATION.yaml.

---

## What Phase 3 Does

Creates:
1. `framework/skills/` — Built-in Skill YAML definitions with use cases
2. `EXTENSION.md` for the framework spoke (may already exist — verify first)
3. Migrates `WAI-Backpressure.yaml` content into `qc-check` Skill override

---

## Pre-Phase Checklist

Before starting Phase 3:
- [ ] On branch `wai-v2-migration`
- [ ] `WAI-MIGRATION.yaml` shows `current_phase: 2` (Phase 2 complete)
- [ ] `hub/WAI-Manifest.yaml` exists
- [ ] `registry/wheelwright/framework/SPOKE.md` exists

---

## Skills That Need To Be Created

Each Skill lives in `framework/skills/{skill-name}.yaml`.

### Required Built-In Skills

| File | Role | Trigger |
|------|------|---------|
| `safe-refactor.yaml` | guardian | pre-structural-change |
| `qc-check.yaml` | reviewer | pre-commit, on-demand |
| `hub-watcher.yaml` | watcher | on-wakeup |
| `framework-updater.yaml` | worker | on-demand |
| `brief-advisor.yaml` | advisor | on-demand |
| `session-observer.yaml` | watcher | on-closeout |
| `file-audit.yaml` | reviewer | on-demand |
| `integration-check.yaml` | guardian | on-wakeup |

### Skill YAML Schema

Every Skill YAML **MUST** include a `use_cases` section with real scenarios. This is non-negotiable — it serves as documentation, agent context, and institutional memory.

```yaml
id: "safe-refactor"
name: "Safe Refactor Guardian"
role: "guardian"
model_tier: "lightweight"          # lightweight | standard | advanced
trigger: "pre_refactor"
scope:
  reads: ["**/*"]
  writes: ["none — read only, fires events"]

description: >
  Ensures a clean git checkpoint exists before any structural code changes.
  If git is dirty, prompts for a commit before proceeding.

use_cases:
  - scenario: "Agent is about to refactor the auth module"
    what_happens: "safe-refactor fires, checks git status, commits if dirty"
    why_it_matters: "If refactoring breaks something, one git revert recovers everything"
    user_trigger: "Automatic — fires on pre_refactor event"

  - scenario: "Hub folder was destroyed by a rogue agent"
    what_happens: "Would have been prevented — checkpoint would exist to revert to"
    why_it_matters: "This actually happened on 2026-02-10. This Skill exists because of it."
    origin: "WAI v2 architectural session, 2026-02-11"

prerequisites:
  - "git must be initialized in the project"

output:
  on_success: "Clean git state confirmed or new commit created"
  on_failure: "Lug created: 'Refactor blocked — uncommitted changes detected'"

tests:
  - name: "Fires on dirty working tree"
    input: "git status shows modified files"
    expected: "Prompts for commit or blocks refactor"
  - name: "Passes on clean tree"
    input: "git status shows nothing to commit"
    expected: "Proceeds without interruption"
```

---

## EXTENSION.md Schema

`EXTENSION.md` describes the identity and behavior of a spoke. Check if it already exists (`EXTENSION.md` at repo root) before creating. If it exists, verify it has all required sections.

Required sections:
```markdown
# {Extension Name}

## Identity
Role: {e.g., Framework — Core implementation and agent tools}
Lens: {How this extension interprets information}

## Behaviors
Always: {What this extension always does}
Never: {What this extension never does}

## Skills Loaded
- safe-refactor (guardian)
- qc-check (reviewer)
- {any project-specific skills}

## Offers
- {What this spoke produces that others may need}

## Subscribes To
- hub:framework:* (framework updates)
```

---

## WAI-Backpressure.yaml Migration

If `WAI-Backpressure.yaml` exists in any spoke:
1. Read its contents
2. Create `{spoke}/skills/qc-check.yaml` with those commands as the skill's check list
3. Add tombstone comment to `WAI-Backpressure.yaml`: `# RETIRED: Migrated to skills/qc-check.yaml as of WAI v2`

---

## Phase 3 Closeout

After all Skills and EXTENSION.md are created:
1. Update `WAI-MIGRATION.yaml`: `current_phase: 3`, add phase 3 to `completed_phases` with commit hash
2. Commit: `"WAI v2 Phase 3: Skills, extension identity, and integration-check created"`
3. Push branch

---

## Verification Checklist

- [ ] `framework/skills/` has all 8 built-in Skill YAMLs
- [ ] Every Skill has `use_cases` section with at least 2 real scenarios
- [ ] Every Skill has `tests` section
- [ ] `EXTENSION.md` exists with all required sections
- [ ] `WAI-Backpressure.yaml` tombstoned (if it existed)
- [ ] `WAI-Manifest.yaml` `skills_loaded` field reflects new skills
- [ ] WAI-MIGRATION.yaml updated with Phase 3 commit hash
